431
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:54,320
Returning to the first discussion May 2023
· Room 510

432
00:33:54,480 --> 00:33:58,580
I have two central questions. One is this:

433
00:33:58,580 --> 00:34:02,090
If we really took it apart,

434
00:34:02,090 --> 00:34:07,160
[unclear], would you be okay with that?

435
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:10,160
Why wouldn't I be?

436
00:34:10,160 --> 00:34:15,160
You said earlier that you wanted everyone
from 510 to appear.

437
00:34:15,160 --> 00:34:22,160
What if we don't go in that direction or
force it? — That's fine.

438
00:34:22,160 --> 00:34:24,160
That's a personal attachment.

439
00:34:24,160 --> 00:34:28,009
I think everyone can share the footage.

440
00:34:28,009 --> 00:34:31,760
Each person's edit could be different.

441
00:34:31,760 --> 00:34:37,760
There doesn't have to be just one film, or
only the thing I imagined.

442
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:44,160
Those two could make their own edit too.
There's plenty of footage.

443
00:34:44,160 --> 00:34:47,160
We could end up with many different films.

444
00:34:47,160 --> 00:34:49,340
You could shoot and edit one too.

445
00:34:49,340 --> 00:34:52,840
Everyone can use the footage to tell their
own story.

446
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:57,316
But when we're producing the footage,

447
00:34:57,316 --> 00:35:02,760
there needs to be some centralized
direction.

448
00:35:02,760 --> 00:35:06,360
So I still have to speak up.

449
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:12,360
For example, you still want the piece to
be performed on stage.

450
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:15,920
But as we work and discover things
together,

451
00:35:15,920 --> 00:35:19,560
the structure of the third part might
change.

452
00:35:19,560 --> 00:35:21,760
[Unclear] Must it come out as planned?

453
00:35:21,760 --> 00:35:23,240
It can change. No problem.

